    {
      "stride": "ElevationOfPrivilege",
      "title": "Shared database account gives editor more rights than the user has",
      "scenario": "The editor needs one database connection to run user-written SQL. If that connection uses a broad or administrative account, a business user inherits its rights: they can read system catalogues, other tenants' schemas, and credential or secret tables, and may call database functions that reach the host or network. The user's dashboard role becomes irrelevant.",
