        "title": "Run user SQL under a least-privilege, read-only role",
        "given": "the reporting dashboard executes user-supplied SQL",
        "when": "a query is sent to the replica",
        "then": "it runs under a dedicated role limited to read-only access on approved reporting objects, with no access to system catalogues, file or network functions"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Tampering",
      "title": "Write or DDL statements change the replica or get replayed to production",
      "scenario": "Nothing in the design limits the editor to SELECT. A user (or an attacker who has a user's session) submits UPDATE, DELETE, DROP or CREATE statements. On a writable replica this corrupts reporting data that the business then trusts; if the replica is ever promoted or the same connection is reused against the primary, the damage reaches production records.",
